        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s04_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s04_c2_first_defines_semantics_aware_notion",
          "text": "First, it defines a semantics-aware notion of adversarial robustness for node-level predictions, and with it a brand new concept for the graph domain called over-robustness, which is robustness against admissible perturbations whose ground-truth label has already changed.",
          "expected_role": "result",
          "cue_keywords": [
